WEBVTT

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:06.370
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:12.370
The reading from the Sinoxadion for May 11 on which we commemorate our Holy Father's

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:20.360
Cyril and Methodius equal to the Apostles and Evangelizers of the Slavs.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:26.560
On this day we celebrate the memory of our Holy Father's Cyril Constantine and Methodius

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:32.040
equal to the Apostles and Evangelizers of the Slavs.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:38.700
These new Apostles were born into a noble family in Thessalonica, a city which, being at the

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:45.600
crossroads of various peoples, had been strongly influenced by the Slavs in the 9th century.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.760
The two brothers had, from childhood, been in contact with the Slav peoples who had settled

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.360
in the region, learning their dialect and becoming used to their customs.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:04.120
The Thodios, the elder, born in 815, was of a calm and gentle character.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:10.240
He acquired a solid legal knowledge and quickly showed such great aptitude for administration

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.760
that he was given the government of a province inhabited by Slavs.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:22.040
He nevertheless realized, after several years, that he should not be wasting time in concern

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:28.760
for things that are not of eternal value and resigned.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:33.880
Fleeing from the world as a sparrow flees the hunter's snare, he reached the prestigious

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:40.640
monastic center of Mount Olympus in Bethinia, where he became an exemplary monk, both by

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:48.640
his obedience and love of prayer, and also his application to the study of the scriptures.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:56.680
Born in 827, was gifted by God with an exceptional intelligence and memory, and dreamed from

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:04.400
his earliest years of espousing not a beautiful princess, but the wisdom of God, like a second

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.200
Solomon.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:12.840
At the age of 14, he had learned the poems of St. Gregory the Theologian by heart, and

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:19.720
begged his teachers with tears to teach him the grammar of the Homeric dialect, so that

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:23.080
he could penetrate their sense.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:28.440
The young boys' talents gained such renown that they were heard of by the all-powerful

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:36.720
Legothetus the Octastus, who summoned him to Constantinople and took him under his protection.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.960
Constantine quickly completed his general studies and was initiated into higher sciences by

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:51.120
the best masters of the time, Leo the mathematician, and St. Fotius, whose beloved disciple he became.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:58.400
With Fotius, he learned where to find true wisdom, the knowledge of things divine and human

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:05.840
which teaches man to conduct himself in all things in the image and likeness of his creator.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:12.480
He was known as the Philosopher, and becoming familiar with the highest court circles was

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:18.800
reckoned by the Octastus to be destined for a brilliant political career, to be inaugurated

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.560
by marriage to one of his nieces.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:28.540
The Philosopher thanked him for his suggestion, but replied that nothing meant anything to him

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:35.600
but to acquire knowledge and to recover the glory lost by our first father.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:42.240
He had, though, to accept ordination to the deaconate and was given the dignity of Kartofelak's

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.440
to patriarch Ignatius.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:52.480
However, he abandoned this situation very soon to withdraw to a monastery on the Bosphorus,

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:59.840
the Glideon, where he met the dethroned iconoclast patriarch John VII Grammaticus and engaged

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:06.280
with him in fiery controversy over the defense of Orthodoxy.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:11.840
After six months, he was recalled to the capital and was forced under pressure from the Octastus

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:16.840
to accept the post of Professor of Philosophy.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:25.640
In 851, when he was 24, the Emperor Michael III sent him on a diplomatic mission to Caliph

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:32.600
Al-Muthawakul, discussions with the Arabs rapidly turned from politics to theology, and

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:38.000
it was with the assurance of the early martyrs that Constantine made an Apologia for the Holy

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:45.680
Trinity before their wise men, showing them the superiority of Christian principles.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:53.400
Barely escaping an attempt to poison him, he was able to return safe and sound to Byzantium.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:59.440
In Caesar Bartus, at Constantine's protector, the Octastus assassinated, in order to take

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:06.080
power in 855, he, again, abandoning the cares of the world to seek wisdom and silence and

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:12.580
prayer, went to join his brother Methodius on Mount Olympus, where they together devoted

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.760
themselves to study.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:22.800
In 860, the Emperor, having consulted with patriarch Fotius, called Constantine back from his

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:29.400
retreat to send him on a mission to the Khan of the Khazars, who had asked him to send

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:35.160
him an educated man to discuss religious matters with the Jews and Arabs who were trying

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.760
to convert his people.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:43.520
Accompanied by his brother, and an imposing entourage, the philosopher learned Hebrew on

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:49.280
the journey and was miraculously given a knowledge of the Samaritan dialect.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:55.160
With the Khazar court, they held long theological discussions with the Jews, and Constantine

00:05:55.160 --> 00:06:01.520
confounded the doctors of the law, showing them the superiority of the gospel, and thus obtaining

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:08.160
the conversion of many dignitaries, and also the freeing of Christian captives.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:14.240
After having signed a treaty of alliance with the Khan, the two brothers set off homeward,

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:19.680
burning on the way the pagan peoples of Tauric Cursonies.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:25.480
They also took St. Clemens' relics, which they had discovered in a miraculous way, in

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:31.640
Cursonises, Stavastopol, back with them to Rome.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:37.480
Immediately after he had given his report to the Emperor, Constantine withdrew into Hisikia

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:41.800
and prayer near the Church of the Holy Apostles.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:47.480
Portias, having refused the episcopal consecration that was offered him, had nevertheless to accept

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:55.320
the post of Abbot of the Monastery of Polycronion, where 70 monks were living at that time.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:07:00.320
This return to their beloved quietude lasted a very short time.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:08.280
In 863, an embassy sent by Rastislav, Prince of Moravia, arrived in Constantinople to ask

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:14.240
the Emperor for a bishop and a teacher capable of instructing them in their language in the

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:21.320
Christian faith that they had initially received in part from Frankish missionaries from Bavaria.

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:26.800
These latter preached in Latin and celebrated a liturgy that was incomprehensible.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:32.840
This resulting in few conversions and the keeping by the people were the most part of their

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:35.360
idolatrous customs.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:37.680
Michael II replied to them,

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:43.640
It is not for me to dictate your faith, and he refused to give them a bishop, not wishing

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:48.880
to usurp this region that was under the jurisdiction of the Pope of Rome.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:54.200
But he promised to send them men capable of instructing them in the doctrine of salvation

00:07:54.200 --> 00:08:00.880
in their own language without seeking to impose the Greek language on them.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:06.680
The philosopher was the only man who possessed all the requisite qualities for this mission,

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:11.720
not only by his wisdom, but also because of his knowledge of the Bulgarian dialect and

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:18.800
the principle languages of the time, Greek, Latin, Hebrew, Arabic, or more precisely the Turkokasar

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:23.520
language, Syriac and Samaritan.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:29.400
The philosopher accepted this mission as a command from God, but asked for some time in which

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:36.280
to prepare, and turning to prayer, as was his custom, he begged of God the revelation of

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:41.920
the script that was capable of rendering the sounds of the Slav language in an acceptable

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:43.520
way.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:49.320
In the same way in which the old covenant was revealed to Moses on Sinai, after a revelation

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:56.680
of God on tablets of stone inscribed by his hand, so Constantine, this second Moses,

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:03.280
believed the revelation of a new alphabet, with which he was able at once to write a Slav

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:09.160
translation of the first verses of the Gospel according to St. John.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:15.040
It was these writings that, after study and correction, became the instrument by which the

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:21.160
Slav peoples, until then barbarians and men of gross habits, were able to be placed by the

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:30.000
holy missionaries in the ranks of civilized peoples, who praised God in their own language.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:35.840
Helped by Methodos and other disciples of Slav origin, St. Constantine urgently translated

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:42.640
the Gospel readings for the whole year, the Divine Liturgy, the Book of Hours, and

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:48.160
the Psalter, and it was thus furnished with the instruments that were vital to their apostolic

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:55.760
work, that the Byzantine missionaries left for Moravia in 863.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:10:01.240
They were received with great honor at Rastus Slav's court, and he put a group of disciples

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:05.560
under their guidance to beat taught the new scriptures.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:11.360
The use of the Slav language in the celebration of the holy mysteries and in preaching, the

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:17.360
faithfulness of their apostolic teaching and the radiant sanctity of the two brothers assured

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:24.240
the rapid success of the mission, and in less than three years they had gathered together

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:31.880
more than a hundred disciples, who in their turn spread the good news throughout the kingdom.

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:39.040
But this success provoked jealousy and opposition from the Frankish missionaries, who, seeing

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:44.640
their influence rapidly overshadowed by that of the Byzantines, denounced them for celebrating

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:51.360
the liturgy in Slavonic, although it was only permitted, they said, in Greek, Latin,

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:53.800
or Hebrew.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:58.120
Once the first foundations of their enterprise had been laid, the two brothers decided

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:04.400
to return to Constantinople, to ordain there their chief disciples.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:10.600
But the road being blocked because of the deterioration of relations between Byzantium and Bulgaria,

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:15.560
they decided to go to Venice and take the sea route.

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:20.480
While the missionaries were waiting to charter a ship, the local clergy took up against them

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:24.840
the same accusations that the Frankish missionaries had used.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:30.360
The matter was referred to Pope Nicholas I who summoned them to Rome.

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:35.800
When they arrived, bearing as a gift the relics of Saint Clement, the people gave them an

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:38.120
enthusiastic welcome.

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:44.320
Pope Adrian II, who had just been elected after the sudden death of Nicholas, approved the

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:50.240
work of the two apostles and solemnly placed their translation of the Holy Books on the

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:57.680
altar of Santa Maria Maggiore, condemning their accusers, the triglycites, three language

00:11:57.680 --> 00:11:59.760
users.

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:05.280
He then himself ordained Methodius and three of their disciples to the priesthood, and

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:10.920
on the following days they were all able to celebrate in Slavonic in many of the city's

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:13.160
churches.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:19.040
During this stay at Rome, Constantin, exhausted by the journeys and labors of the mission,

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:26.520
fell seriously ill, and on the 14th of February in 869, after having received the monastic

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:34.800
habit under the name Cyril, gave his apostolic soul into God's hands, praying for the confirmation

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:39.320
of the Slav peoples in the Orthodox faith.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:45.280
He was buried with great honor in the Basilica of St. Clement, and miracles were later worked

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.920
at his tomb.

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:54.600
Kosoel, prince of Pannonia, admiring the work of these Byzantine missionaries in Moravia

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:59.760
and himself desiring to remove his people from the influence of the Bavarian missionaries

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:04.960
from Pusau, had suggested to them when they passed through his country on the way to Venice

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:09.400
that he can fight to them the formation of 50 disciples.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:15.080
Shortly after St. Cyril's death, Kosoel sent messengers to Rome, asking that Methodius

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:21.960
be sent to him without delay, and Pope Adrian exceeded to this request.

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:28.160
After a highly successful first mission, Methodius returned to Rome to the Pope to be consecrated

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:36.360
Bishop of Syrmium, now Stremska Mitrovica, a sea that had been founded earlier by the Holy

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:43.520
Apostle Andronicus, with jurisdiction not only over Pannonia, but all the Slav peoples of

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:49.640
Central Europe, with whose conversion he was entrusted in 870.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:56.640
In the midst of afflictions and labors, the saint unstinctingly continued his work of evangelization,

00:13:56.640 --> 00:14:02.600
as his main teaching instrument that translated divine liturgy which gave the Neophytes the nourishment

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:05.680
necessary for their spiritual growth.

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:12.000
He ordained priests and deacons, and, thanks to his administrative experience, was able

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:17.640
to give this new church the canonical foundations of its organization.

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:24.760
But when he arrived in Moravia in 873, the situation had greatly changed.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:31.560
His vetoplock had seized power after having Rastislav blinded, and had once again given the

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:34.760
country over to German influence.

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:41.800
Methodius had only just arrived when he was arrested and made to appear before Asinid in Bavaria,

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:48.480
which, after a travesty of a judgment, had him shut in a tower in Suav, where he suffered

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:52.920
cruelly from the rigors of the climate.

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:58.880
It was only after two and a half years that Pope John VIII was advised of the situation

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:02.000
and was able to set the saint free.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:08.040
As soon as he returned to Moravia, Methodius took up his work again with increased zeal,

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:12.040
ignoring the ban against celebrating the liturgy in Slavonic.

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:18.760
He did not hesitate to reprimand Svetoplock severely for his ill-regulated behavior, and

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:25.160
uncompromisingly opposed the erroneous doctrine of the Filioque, which the Frankish clergy

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:29.320
were attempting to impose in this missionary land.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:36.280
The Franks appealed to Rome, but Methodius, within Apologia to the Pope for his actions,

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:44.080
in 879, returned in triumph with the confirmation of all his rights, to the confusion of his sworn

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:48.560
enemy leaking the suffrage in Bishop of Nida.

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:54.240
The latter never seized his intrigues, a next time accused the saint of rebellion against

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:56.000
the Emperor.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:02.240
This new trial was for Methodius an opportunity to travel to Constantinople to give Emperor

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:09.760
Basil the First and Patriarch Fotius news of his mission and to assure them of his unshakeable

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:13.640
faithfulness in 881.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:19.360
He was received at court with great deference, and both sovereign and patriarch strongly

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:24.640
approved the mission and work of the new apostles.

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:31.360
Comforted by this support from the Great Church, Methodius returned to Moravia with his disciples.

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:37.320
And it was in peace and tranquility with no more interference from the Frankish clergy

00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:42.720
that they continued their translation of the Church's books.

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:48.640
Methodius completed the translation of the whole Bible in six months, together with

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:55.840
patristic texts and books of the Holy Cannons, all of which were necessary to the Slav Church

00:16:55.840 --> 00:17:00.920
for its assimilation of the Byzantine Christian heritage.

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:07.580
Once this work was completed, Methodius gathered his disciples together and celebrated a solemn

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:11.040
liturgy and honor of Saint Demetrius.

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:20.160
He then appointed his successor, Saint Gorast, who a native of Moravia had acquired a perfect

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:28.560
knowledge of Greek, and after having blessed the kings and the people gave his soul to God

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:34.200
in peace on the 6th of April in 885.

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:41.200
His funeral was solemnized in Greek, Latin, and Slavonic in the presence of an uncountable

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:48.280
crowd that accompanied him with candles, weeping for their master and good shepherd who had

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:57.280
made himself all things to all men in order to lead them all to salvation.

00:17:57.280 --> 00:18:04.000
The disappearance of the Apostle of the Slavs gave, wicking, and his adherence the opportunity

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:08.260
to resume their conspiracy against the Byzantine missionaries.

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:14.040
He got to Rome before Gorast and succeeded in convincing Pope Stephen V of Methodius'

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:20.520
heterodoxy, and it was armed with a letter giving him with full powers that he returned

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:22.800
to Moravia.

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:28.800
With the support of Svetloplok, who had little interest in theological matters, the felon

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:33.600
launched a merciless persecution of Methodius' disciples.

00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:38.960
Gorast, Clement, and more than 200 other Holy Confessers.

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:42.480
Some were beaten and dragged through briars.

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:48.800
The youngest were sold as slaves to Venetian merchants, and others were exiled to the furthest

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:52.940
extremities of the kingdom.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:19:02.260
Gorast found refuge in Poland, others in Bohemia, and Clement, Nahum, Savus, Angelarius,

00:19:02.260 --> 00:19:11.660
and Lawrence managed to reach Bulgaria, where they were welcomed as angels of God by Zarboris.

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:19.340
Their persecutors found just punishment for their conduct, because in 907 Moravia was invaded

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:30.070
and ravaged by the Hungarians, passing definitively from then on under Latin domination.

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:36.270
The work of the two brothers equal to the apostles Cyril and Methodius left no trace on

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.030
this earth.

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:44.750
But through the intermediary of the Bulgarian church, it became the seed of a rich Byzantine

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:54.070
tradition that found its apogee in Kievan Russia after the conversion of St. Vladimir.

00:19:54.070 --> 00:20:00.710
Through the prayers of our Holy Fathers, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us and

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:01.350
save us.
